sg-session (0.1.0-190) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sg-brokerd: LogonUser's password check (wine-sg 1709). The "@logon"
    request checks an account's password with PAM, in the root monitor as
    for elevation, and answers with a one-time ticket: a file in
    /run/stained-glass-broker/tickets (the SYSTEM account's alone) naming
    the account, the requester and a 30-second limit. The machine
    wineserver turns the ticket into the token. The password is never
    written anywhere and is wiped once checked. Root and the SYSTEM account
    cannot be logged on to. Test: make test-logon-ticket, mutant
    SG_MUTANT_LOGON_NO_PASSWORD_CHECK.

