sg-session (0.1.0-163) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: the shared Wine folders' own entries are the system's. Every
    person is in the Wine group and the folders were group-writable without
    the sticky bit: anyone could rename the prefix away, replace
    dosdevices\c: (SYSTEM's services would load C:\windows from a folder of
    theirs), replace the registry files and markers, or plant a stamp that
    skips a protection. /var/lib/stained-glass, the prefix, state and
    .local are sticky; dosdevices is the system's alone; what a person put
    among the system's files is moved aside at boot (their own agent socket
    and session file stay); the system's files there are not the group's to
    change (sg_shared_state_hardened; test/shared-state-test.sh, mutant
    SG_MUTANT_SHARED_STATE_OPEN). wine-sg 1475 refuses a hive the server did
    not write.

