sg-session (0.1.0-162) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remote Desktop: frames go compressed. An encoder of our own for RDP 6.0
    bitmap compression ("planar", MS-RDPEGDI 2.2.2.5.1), lossless: vertical
    deltas and run-length coding per colour plane, no alpha plane. Used when
    the client advertises it (Windows' client and FreeRDP do), uncompressed
    otherwise. A desktop of application windows costs a tenth of what it did,
    a scrolled page of text a seventh; a photographic wallpaper about half.
    Gate: make test-rdp-stream (build/planar-test against FreeRDP's decoder,
    then pixel-exact through a real client over gradients and scrolling text,
    planar and uncompressed); mutant SG_MUTANT_PLANAR_DELTA.

